==Trivia==
* This card's immersive illustration from {{TCGP|Genetic Apex}} includes {{p|Caterpie}}, {{p|Butterfree}}, {{p|Weedle}}, {{p|Pidgey}}, {{p|Pikachu}}, {{p|Nidoran♀}}, {{p|Nidoran♂}}, {{p|Oddish}}, {{p|Poliwag}}, and {{p|Ponyta}}.
* This card's immersive illustration from {{TCGP|Deluxe Pack: ex}} includes Pokémon appearing on the booster packs of [[List of Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket expansions|previous expansions]]: {{p|Mewtwo}}, {{p|Charizard}}, {{p|Pikachu}} (Genetic Apex); {{p|Mew}} ({{TCGP|Mythical Island}}); {{p|Dialga}}, {{p|Palkia}} ({{TCGP|Space-Time Smackdown}}); {{p|Arceus}} ({{TCGP|Triumphant Light}}); {{Shiny}} {{p|Beedrill}}, Shiny {{p|Pachirisu}}, Shiny {{p|Lucario}}, Shiny {{p|Varoom}} ({{TCGP|Shining Revelry}}); {{p|Solgaleo}}, {{p|Lunala}} ({{TCGP|Celestial Guardians}}); {{p|Nihilego}}, {{p|Buzzwole}}, {{p|Guzzlord}}, {{p|Blacephalon}} ({{TCGP|Extradimensional Crisis}}); {{p|Eevee}}, {{p|Vaporeon}}, {{p|Jolteon}}, {{p|Flareon}}, {{p|Espeon}}, {{p|Umbreon}}, {{p|Leafeon}}, {{p|Glaceon}}, {{p|Sylveon}} ({{TCGP|Eevee Grove}}); {{p|Ho-Oh}}, {{p|Lugia}} ({{TCGP|Wisdom of Sea and Sky}}); and {{p|Suicune}} ({{TCGP|Secluded Springs}}).
* This is the first card in [[Pokémon Trading Card Game Pocket]] to have multiple immersive prints.

===Origin===
*'''Circle Circuit''' is an attack that first appeared on {{TCG ID|XY|Raichu|43}} from the {{TCG|XY}} expansion. The only other TCG card with Circle Circuit is {{TCG ID|SWSH Promo|Pikachu V|63}}, one of the {{TCG|SWSH Black Star Promos}}.

